{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "10", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "00", "M": "50", "S": "45"}}, "news": [{"title": "Pune town planning schemes\u2019 future in the dark as state cancels plans", "para": "Pune's town planning schemes face a bleak outlook as the state government has paused their progression. Some of these projects were already in the land acquisition phase, and the recent transition of two schemes in Uruli-Phursungi to a different municipal council only adds to the uncertainty. Urban development experts argue that this move could hinder the city's urgent urbanisation goals, even as other plans await action from PMRDA.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/pune-town-planning-schemes-future-in-the-dark-as-state-cancels-plans/133063374?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-39104/133063374.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Freehold relief in sight for Chandigarh\u2019s leasehold properties", "para": "The Ministry of Home Affairs is currently reviewing a proposal to convert leasehold properties to freehold status. This pivotal development emerges after extensive discussions among political figures and ministers. The Chandigarh administration, having secured the needed approvals, forwarded this proposal. It is anticipated that this change will enhance property values and stimulate investment within the city, along with providing updates on other property-related matters.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/freehold-relief-in-sight-for-chandigarhs-leasehold-properties/133063350?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-272616/133063350.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Registration opens for 460 plots in Lucknow development body's Anant Nagar", "para": "Online registration for 460 plots in Lucknow's Anant Nagar scheme is now open.  These plots, ranging from 112.5 to 200 square metres, will be allotted through a lottery.  The Anant Nagar scheme is being developed along Mohan Road with wide roads and green spaces.  LDA will also conduct a lottery for 407 housing units on August 14.  Previously, the authority allotted 75 flats in Park View and Aishbagh Square apartments.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/registration-opens-for-460-plots-in-lucknow-development-bodys-anant-nagar/133063254?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-263930/133063254.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}]}